# vukem-video

A video editor operated by commands: the CLI `vukem-video`, or the MCP server (`vukem-video mcp`) with the same operations as tools. Output is text; `--json` is JSON.

Check with `project:list`. The workspace is `~/.vukem-video` or `$VUKEM_VIDEO_HOME`. `serve` shares it with the browser.

## The loop

1. Read: `project:show --project <id>` (text; note `rev`).
2. Plan a batch.
3. Apply: `edit --project <id> --base <rev> ...`; read the diff.
4. `lint --project <id>`. Errors block export.
5. Look only if text cannot: `view --at 1s`, then `view --mode sheet`.
6. `export --project <id>`, then check `lint` and the `checks` of the job.

## Rules that prevent mistakes

- Every time has a unit: `12.5s`, `375f`, `00:00:12.500`. A bare number is rejected.
- Ids (`prj_`, `ast_`, `trk_`, `itm_`, `job_`) are never positions. List first.
- The top track is drawn over the others (ends: `top`, `bottom`).
- `--base` is the `revision` of your last result; omitted, the current one.
- Give your own `id` to what a batch creates that later operations use.

